## Step 1 — Capture unresolved items (all sessions)
Auto-file every unresolved item this session surfaced as its own Notion Team-Tasks ticket, for future discussion. Do NOT ask Erez to weigh in on, approve, or apply any of them during the wrap — file silently; the Step 7 report's past-tense list of what was filed is required and is not "discussing" them. This step runs in every session (it is not project-gated; a global-only session still runs it — it is not one of the project-specific steps Step 0 skips). It **overrides, for capture-only [-filing and-]{+filing,+} for the on-demand ref-file appends in sub-step [-(3),**-]{+(3), and for the weekly size check's ticket filing and raising (config-health `size-weekly.md`),**+} the standing rules "Before creating or materially changing a ticket in a tracker, draft the full proposal" and "On \"apply learnings\"" (their approval-before-filing gates) — it does **not** override approval for applying a learning to any other home (`CLAUDE.md`, a skill, a hook's code; those still need `/check` + Erez's approval in a future session), and it does not change the assignee logic in sub-step 7.

**Every Team-Tasks write this step and Step 3c make goes through the ticket-quality gate (GEN-508), UNATTENDED (GEN-702).** The gate hard-blocks every Team-Tasks create / duplicate / move / substantive-body edit unless a single-use pass minted by an independent review exists, so each write here — the create in sub-step 7 (and, if the GEN-145 symptom appears, its in-place body repair), the near-duplicate body append in sub-step 6, and Step 3c's create and append — is filed by running the `/vet-ticket` machinery: **reference that skill's flow, do not re-specify it here.** Per item, run it unattended: draft the payload — set `Urgency`/`Gain ratio`/`Priority` per `/vet-ticket` Step 1, which treats a create and a material body append alike (both are material, so both derive these fields) → get its `contentHash` per `/vet-ticket` Step 1 → spawn ONE independent `check-reviewer` against the ticket bar (`/vet-ticket` Step 2) → resolve any notes, then write the ticket-record (`/vet-ticket` Steps 3–4), with `source` set to `wrap-step1` for this step's writes and `wrap-step3c` for Step 3c's → run the `/vet-ticket` Step 7 evidence precondition → mint the single-use ticket pass → issue the Notion write → re-fetch and confirm it landed (`/vet-ticket` Step 8). **No Erez-facing card:** Steps 1 and [-3c-]{+3c, and the weekly size check (which uses `source` `wrap-step1`),+} carry the standing override exempting them from the draft-for-approval pause, so `/vet-ticket` Step 5's card is skipped and the mint proceeds silently; the Step 6 waive lane needs Erez and is therefore unavailable here. `check-reviewer` has no Notion tool, so the near-duplicate search is NOT its job on this lane — sub-steps 5–6 already did it before drafting; the reviewer judges only ticket quality against its bar.

**Bounded — an unattended filing must never loop or hang the wrap.** If the reviewer does not return a clean PASS, amend the drafted payload per its findings and re-review with a fresh `check-reviewer` (re-hashing first) — but cap this at **2 further review rounds** (count every round that does not end in a clean PASS, not only literal REVISE verdicts). If the cap is reached, OR the item is blocked on information only Erez holds, OR any step of the machinery hard-errors (a non-zero `--ticket-hash` exit, a mint or evidence-precondition failure, a post-mint apply failure such as `consume-failed` or a Notion API error, a sidecar/transcript read failure — illustrative, not exhaustive: any hard error stops it) → do NOT force-file and do NOT loop. Leave the item unfiled, surface it in the Step 7 report **with enough substance to act on later**, and record it durably so a gate-blocked capture is not lost — in the Step 4 HISTORY.md entry (per Step 4 sub-step 2) when this wrap logs a project, or, when the wrap logs no project so Step 4 is skipped (Step 0), in a dated recovery file `C:\Users\Erez\.claude\wrap-surfaced-not-filed-<timestamp>.md` whose path the Step 7 report then names (Step 1 runs in every session, so its durability is unconditional too) — for a later manual `/vet-ticket`. Once a recovery file's items have all been filed, rename it to `wrap-surfaced-filed-<same timestamp>.md` rather than deleting it; Step 3i reports recovery files not yet renamed. **A surfaced-not-filed item counts as a note the steps require surfacing**, so it forces the full Step 7 report (never the all-clean fast-path). (Same posture as sub-step 7's GEN-145 handling: once, do not loop.)

